            "review_title": "Review at Lau De Truong Dinh",
            "review_text": "Sue P\nKent, United Kingdom51 contributions\n0\nReal authentic Vietnamese food – hard to find in Saigon!\nJan 2015 • Couples\nSaigon was our last port of call during our 12 day tour of Vietnam - and our least favourite place - but this restaurant made me feel that we had discovered a little bit of the city that still catered for us folks wishing to eat authentic Vietnamese food - admittedly you must be able to eat goat. From the time we arrived the waiter really looked after us - helped us cook the barbeque starter, showed us how to use the dips with fresh leaves, and cooked our pot of goat brains, marrow & liver - which was lovely (cant believe I am saying that - if you had asked me to eat that a few weeks ago I would have heaved!) Yes, we were the only non Vietnamese people in the restaurant and we loved it! All 6 of us said it helped make our stay in Saigon worth it. We also ordered goat ribs but they had run out, then noticed at the bottom of the menu it said \"Goats Gonads - not for the faint hearted\" .... we ordered it, but our wonderful waiter showed it to us uncooked on a platter .... it was the whole undercarriage .... we decided that maybe were fainted hearted after all and so declined !! For a great Vietnamese evening in Saigon this place is a must - Also great price & beer too!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 5, 2015",
