            "review_text": "malleebull\nMelbourne, Australia33 contributions\n0\nPleasant surprise\nJan 2015\nAfter looking around for a place to eat, we (a family of four) stumbled on to this inconspicuous place and reluctantly went in. No westerners in sight! Just locals sitting on plastic chairs around gas cookers enjoying themselves. We sat down not having a clue what to order or do. We were shown a menu with some pictures and chose the goat meat option. The waiter demonstrated what we needed to do. Basically cook the goat meat and okra, then wrap it in rice paper with some leaves and dip it in a coconut sauce ( add chilli if you want and eat it). Our young boys really enjoyed the experience and so did I. With some water the total bill was about 168,000 vnd. A very pleasant surprise.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 18, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
