            "review_title": "Review at Lau De Truong Dinh",
            "review_text": "doctordonn\nBangkok, Thailand118 contributions\n0\naweful\nApr 2013 • Friends\nLiving in SE Asia since 2001 I have had many occasions when my friends or co-workers have taken me out for some strange exotic food in a hole-in-the-wall place where I was the only westerner for kilometers around. More often than not the food was delicious and the cultural experience unforgettable. In this way I have been pleasantly surprised that I could not only keep down, but actually enjoy, dishes such as fried crickets, roast dog, duck blood pudding, field rats, and coconut worms. Lau De Truong Dinh, unfortunately, was not such an experience. Greasy, chewy goat meat in a thin porridge gruel. I survived the evening on Saigon Beer and peanuts. I have had goat other times at other places and, while it is not my favorite food, I can usually manage to eat it. If your Vietnamese friends want to take you here, best to feign an upset stomach and politely decline.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 24, 2013",
